  "about": [
    "Key corpus for detectKey: chord progressions with a labelled home key.",
    "No entry carries a key hint; detection has to work from the chords alone.",
    "`key` is the tonic with an `m` for minor. A relative major/minor confusion counts as wrong.",
    "`anyMode` entries have no third on the tonic chord, so only the tonic is checked.",
    "`hard` marks progressions that are ambiguous by nature; they are allowed to be the misses.",
    "Labels come from harmonic analysis of the progression, not from a recording."
